  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "With no prior experiments completed, the most critical uncertainty is the baseline performance of the simplest viable model. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the most minimal configuration: a single-profile RNA model with the standard PCA representation and no aggregation or fusion steps. Running this first establishes a reference accuracy/F1 against which every subsequent design decision (multiprofile aggregation, learned RNA encoders like scVI/scGPT, image modality, and multimodal fusion) can be meaningfully compared. It is also the fastest to train, giving quick signal under a limited budget. Without this anchor, any later experiment's performance would be uninterpretable—we could not tell whether a multimodal or multiprofile setup is genuinely adding information or merely adding complexity. This single experiment reduces the most fundamental uncertainty in the search space."
}

